  "description": "Patterns on the track network: nodes a (512, 1536) to i (8704, 1536), a tile apart, joined by straight edges e1 a-b to e8 h-i, each 1024 long, dead ends at both ends. A (1536, 512), B (3584, 512), C (5632, 512) and D (7680, 512) each have a platform on the half tile of track either side of their node, b, d, f and h, so a train stops at the node going either way and drives as far from call to call as it did on the grid. Main calls at A, B, C, D and plans its legs with a crawl, { acceleration 250, braking 250, topSpeed 1 } (Stage W2c, ARCHITECTURE decision 40): 2048 units take 4 + 111.2 + 4 s, so 120, and 6144 4 + 341.6 + 4, so 350. A service's journey starts at the berth that makes the shortest round trip, the end of its first call's platform past the node going east, 512 units on, so its first leg is 512 shorter: 1536 units in 91 s, 5632 in 321. Main's round trip is 91 + 5 x 120 s of travel, 1 minute at B and C each way and 2 at each end, 1171 s, rounded up to 20 minutes, as before; peak 5 trains 4 apart, off-peak 2 (10 apart), low none. Pattern 0 is a short working B-C (91 + 120 s and 2 + 2 minutes, 451 s, round trip 8, at most 4 trains); pattern 1 an express A-D that passes B and C (321 s out and 350 back, round trip 911 s, rounded up to 16 minutes, at most 8). A train sent out from the node drives the whole 2048 or 6144. addLinePattern needs two calls or more, rising, each a stop of the line; setLineStops may not leave a pattern calling past the new last stop. A segment carries at most 720 trains a day each way (one every 2 minutes); a service puts a day's trains at its headway, rounded up, on each segment from its first call to its last, and the services claim room in order, the line's own first. At peak Main puts 360 on every segment; pattern 0 would run 4 trains 2 apart (720) on B-C, but only 360 is left there, so it runs 2, 4 apart; nothing is left on B-C for the express, which runs none. Off-peak: Main 144, pattern 0 one train 8 apart (180), the express one train 16 apart (90). Low: Main runs none; pattern 0 keeps a 20-minute target, one train (72), so A-B and C-D are not covered. Shuttle, at B facing east on pattern 0, is sent out at 480 and every 8 minutes until 600, the first off-peak minute (Stage W2b: it leaves 42 s after it is sent out, its 6-minute trip brings it back 42 s after the minute, its service ends once it has dwelt 42 s there, and it is sent out again at the next minute). The express waits through the peak, is sent out from A at 600, off-peak, and leaves at 600:42, with a timetable calling only at A and D: at D at 606:32, 350 s later. Removing pattern 0 at 601 takes Shuttle off the line; it finishes its trip as an ordinary service, back at B at 606:42 and ending at 607:24. The express becomes pattern 0.",
